**Yes.** The CLI shortcut for this setting isn't reliable across `az` versions, so use a template deployment from Cloud Shell. It is the same thing as the Portal custom template, so the policy passes.

```bash
az account set --subscription 494e3888-fedb-4a07-96a6-65408b12c0ea

cat > law.json <<'EOF'
{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.OperationalInsights/workspaces",
      "apiVersion": "2022-10-01",
      "name": "log-cn-stg-uaenorth",
      "location": "uaenorth",
      "properties": {
        "sku": { "name": "PerGB2018" },
        "retentionInDays": 30,
        "features": { "disableLocalAuth": true },
        "workspaceCapping": { "dailyQuotaGb": 1 }
      }
    }
  ]
}
EOF

az deployment group create \
  --subscription 494e3888-fedb-4a07-96a6-65408b12c0ea \
  -g PZI-GX-P-RGP-MDCL-P002 \
  -n law-deploy \
  --template-file law.json
```

`retentionInDays` (30) is a placeholder, not the GCP compliance value, so replace it before running. `dailyQuotaGb` (1) is a cost cap.

**Verify:**
```bash
az monitor log-analytics workspace show -g PZI-GX-P-RGP-MDCL-P002 -n log-cn-stg-uaenorth --query "{loc:location,state:provisioningState,localAuthDisabled:features.disableLocalAuth,tags:tags}" -o json
```
Expect `uaenorth`, `Succeeded`, `true`, and `ghs-*` tags.

If it fails, paste the full error, since it will name the policy.

**Rollback:** `az monitor log-analytics workspace delete -g PZI-GX-P-RGP-MDCL-P002 -n log-cn-stg-uaenorth --yes` (soft-deleted for 14 days).

Note: the file `law.json` disappears when the session ends, which is fine, but keep a copy in the repo under `azure/infra/` so the setup is reproducible.
